This repository was established from a Gitea fork. The gitsss product name,
interface, runtime module and release artifacts are independently maintained.
Compatibility code reads existing Gitea configuration and data formats solely
to support administrator-controlled migration. gitsss is not affiliated with
or endorsed by the Gitea project.

Platform baseline: Gitea v1.26.2, commit
2c749ce548b1da0a52835861a87b888e67842d29. The source was copied into this
repository and is maintained under the gitsss module; it is not consumed as a
Gitea application library. Upstream automation directories were not imported.

Actions runner baseline: Gitea Runner v1.0.0, commit
594c9ade7cccf7be6cd0f1cd18ae8d28bba878c2. Its MIT-licensed source and
license are retained under runner/ and maintained as the independent
github.com/neko233-com/gitsss/runner module. The runner is an internal gitsss
service and is not published as a compatibility command.
The server workflow parser reuses this same repository-local act source; no
external Gitea act module or duplicate execution core is linked.

Actions protocol baseline: actions-proto-go v0.4.1. Its generated Connect and
Protocol Buffers source and MIT license are retained under
packages/actions-proto-go and maintained as the independent
github.com/neko233-com/gitsss/packages/actions-proto-go module.

Migration API baseline: Gitea SDK v0.24.1. Its MIT-licensed source is retained
under packages/migration-sdk and maintained as the independent
github.com/neko233-com/gitsss/packages/migration-sdk module. It is used only to
read administrator-selected Gitea migration sources.

Static analysis baseline: gitea-vet v0.2.3. Its MIT-licensed source is retained
under tools/gitsss-vet, adapted to gitsss module boundaries, and maintained as
github.com/neko233-com/gitsss/tools/gitsss-vet.

The single-image Actions bundle includes actions/checkout v4.3.1 at commit
34e114876b0b11c390a56381ad16ebd13914f8d5. Its MIT license and published
runtime files are retained under actions/builtin/actions/checkout/v4.

The bundle also includes gitsss-owned MIT compatibility actions for
`actions/setup-node` v4-v7 and `actions/setup-go` v4-v6. They select the
Node.js 24 and Go 1.26 toolchains embedded in the image, fail closed for
unavailable versions, and never download toolchains at workflow runtime.

The bundle retains the published MIT runtime files for actions/cache v6 at
commit 55cc8345863c7cc4c66a329aec7e433d2d1c52a9,
actions/upload-artifact v7 at commit
043fb46d1a93c77aae656e7c1c64a875d1fc6a0a, and actions/download-artifact v8
at commit 3e5f45b2cfb9172054b4087a40e8e0b5a5461e7c. Supported older major
references are served by these immutable Node.js 24 copies.

The retained upstream copyright notices in LICENSE are legal attribution only
and are not product branding.
